@@ -22,3 +22,12 @@ are ISO-8601 date-time strings, and they are equal until the task's first change
 renaming, tagging or untagging a task sets `updatedAt`; a change that does nothing (renaming a task to the
 title it already has, or tagging it with a tag it already has) leaves it alone. `createTodoList` stamps
 tasks with the system clock, and takes a `now` option to read the time from elsewhere, for example in tests.
+
+Tasks can also be added in bulk with `importTasks(list, text)`, for teams moving over from a spreadsheet. The
+text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`: the priority may be left empty for a normal one, and
+the tags are separated by spaces, for example `Renew the insurance;high;admin money`. Blank lines are skipped,
+and CRLF line endings are accepted. Each valid line is added, and the call returns `{ imported, rejected }`:
+`imported` counts the tasks added, and `rejected` lists every line that was not added as `{ line, reason }`,
+with `line` counting from 1 (blank lines included). A line is rejected when it does not have exactly three
+fields, when its title is empty or a title is already in the list, or when its priority is not `low`,
+`normal` or `high`. A rejected line does not stop the others from being added.
